From 8b8202e17943f0127fb96f00f9da713e273120d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <107831991+SyntaxError-PEBKAC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:25:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] ducksteps: track build files that were never committed

Four files the build depends on existed only in the working tree. None
was covered by .gitignore, and git log --all shows none of them was ever
committed, so they were not deliberately excluded - they were missed.

  * browser/branding/ducksteps/setup.ico
    installer.nsi, uninstaller.nsi and maintenanceservice_installer.nsi
    each !define MUI_ICON setup.ico. No other branding directory carries
    one, on disk or in the index, so this is a ducksteps-specific
    installer icon that existed in exactly one place.

  * build/pgo/pgo_training_extension/manifest.json
    build/pgo/pgo_done.html
    profileserver.py loads build/pgo/pgo_training_extension as a
    WebExtension, and a WebExtension without its manifest cannot load.
    background.js, in the same directory, was already tracked - only its
    manifest was not. pgo_done.html is what background.js navigates to
    at the end of training to shut down cleanly.

  * package.sh
    The PACKAGE phase runs it directly (orchestrator.py invokes
    source_dir / "package.sh" under msys2 bash).

Nothing here changes behaviour. Line endings are kept exactly as found:
the two PGO files are CRLF, matching background.js beside them, and
package.sh is LF, as a script run under bash needs to be. The only edit
to any content is in manifest.json, where a lone tab indented "storage"
while every line around it used spaces.

The exposure was not the build, which kept working because git stash
leaves untracked files alone, so STASH/CHECKOUT/REBASE never disturbed
them. It was everything else: git clean -fdx would have deleted all four
with no way back, a fresh clone could neither package nor run PGO
training, and Patches/*.patch is generated from commits, so anyone
rebuilding ducksteps from upstream plus the published patch stack got a
tree with no installer icon and no package.sh. publish.py already copied
the two PGO files into the docs repo under Docs/PGO/, so those at least
existed off-machine; setup.ico and package.sh existed nowhere else.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 browser/branding/ducksteps/setup.ico          | Bin 0 -> 105143 bytes
 build/pgo/pgo_done.html                       |   2 ++
 .../pgo/pgo_training_extension/manifest.json  |  19 ++++++++++++
 package.sh                                    |  28 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 49 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 browser/branding/ducksteps/setup.ico
 create mode 100644 build/pgo/pgo_done.html
 create mode 100644 build/pgo/pgo_training_extension/manifest.json
 create mode 100644 package.sh

diff --git a/browser/branding/ducksteps/setup.ico b/browser/branding/ducksteps/setup.ico
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5d84472954256ef69a7496b761478dae4d81fb79
GIT binary patch
